{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Elohei ha-Elohim va-Adonei ha-Adonim.</b> Meaning: Elohei ha-Elohim means the Elohim of the angels who are called Elohim, as it is written (Job 1:6) ״וַיָּבֹאוּ בְּנֵי הָאֱלֹהִים״. <b>וַאֲדֹנֵי הָאֲדֹנִים</b> — these are the rulers of the lower world, in the manner of what it says (Genesis 42:30) ״דִּבֶּר הָאִישׁ אֲדֹנֵי הָאָרֶץ״. And it was necessary to state also the specification of the lordship of those below, to make known that earthly lords — a person does not have free choice to do as they please and desire, but He is master over them to turn them to whatever He wishes, and this is the statement of Solomon (Proverbs 21:1) ״לֶב מֶלֶךְ בְּיַד ה׳״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:28.041160136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}